## 3. Commercial Incorporation Requires Separate Authorization

**3.1. Commercial License Required.** You may not engage in Commercial Incorporation
unless you first obtain a Commercial License from the Licensor.

**3.2. No Implied Commercial Rights.** Public availability of the Software, access to its
source code, community participation, or acceptance of a contribution does not grant
permission for Commercial Incorporation.

**3.3. Hosted and SaaS Offerings.** The requirement in Section 3.1 applies to hosted
services, SaaS offerings, and similar services where the Software or a Modification is
incorporated into or forms part of the service offered to Third Parties, even if customers
do not receive a copy of the Software.

**3.4. Independent Products.** You do not need a Commercial License merely because you
used ProxyMaxx internally to develop, test, debug, or inspect an independent product that
does not incorporate the Software or a Modification.

**3.5. Commercial Terms.** A Commercial License must specify the permitted scope of use
and any applicable royalties, fees, attribution requirements, reporting obligations, and
other conditions. No particular royalty rate is established by this Community License, and
no royalty is payable for any use authorized by Section 2.

## 4. Modifications, Patches, and Forks

**4.1. Private Modifications.** You may modify the Software for personal use and Internal
Use, subject to the restrictions in this License.

**4.2. Patch Distribution.** You may publish and distribute Patches for the Software,
provided that:

(a) each Patch is distributed with this License or a reference to it and applicable
attribution information;

(b) the Patch satisfies each requirement of Section 1.5;

(c) you do not remove or misrepresent applicable copyright or licensing notices; and

(d) the Patch is not distributed or used in a manner that constitutes unauthorized
Commercial Incorporation.

**4.3. Complete Modified Forks.** This License does not authorize you to publish,
distribute, or sublicense a complete modified copy or fork of the Software. Any such
distribution requires separate written permission from the Licensor.

**4.4. No Circumvention.** You may not divide a complete modified fork or the Original
Software into multiple files, packages, patches, or downloads for the purpose of
circumventing Section 4.3 or the content restrictions of a Patch in Section 1.5.

**4.5. Contributions.** Submission of a Patch or contribution does not, by itself, transfer
ownership of your contribution to the Licensor or grant you additional rights in the
Software. Contributions may be subject to a separate contribution agreement.

